From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wave: own device, DMA, IRQ and control lifetimes

Keep terminal quiesce, native confirmations, serialized VAP destruction and
TXMM payload completion under their real owners. Retain data-pool totals and
early-failure register guards; omit temporary IRQ/MMIO sampling. Preserve the
native fatal dump before terminal reset, serialize card-index-only replies,
and consume statistics replies before returning their TXMM payloads.

This is the final native integration against the pinned vendor source.
Firmware-dependent policy remains downstream with exact image admission.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

